/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:50:Grow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:51:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:52:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:53:- bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:54:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:55:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:56:- Each arm tip launches a "turtle" heading 90° right of its outward direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:57:- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:58:- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:59:- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:60:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:61:Key insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.
