/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:67:Fire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; mark collisions with maroon or blue.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:68:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:69:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:70:- bg = most common color. Non-bg 3-pixel sprites shaped as axis-aligned L's or diagonal V's.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:71:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:72:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:73:- Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:74:- A projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex in the emission direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:75:- If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:76:- If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:77:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:78:Key insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.
