/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:102:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:103:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:104:- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:105:- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:106:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:107:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:108:- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:109:- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:110:- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. 
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:111:- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:112:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:113:Key insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.
