/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:138:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:139:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:140:- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:141:- Red components outside structures.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:142:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:143:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:144:- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:145:- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:146:- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:147:- Unmatched reds vanish.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:148:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:149:Key insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.
