/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:174:Simulate water falling from top-edge sources, pooling on shelves, and cascading off edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:175:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:176:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:177:- bg = most common color; water = rarest non-bg; shelf = other non-bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:178:- Sources: water clusters touching top row. Shelves: horizontal segments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:179:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:180:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:181:- Water falls down from sources, painting bg cells as water.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:182:- On hitting a shelf, it spreads across the shelf span plus one cell past each end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:183:- From those overflow positions, water resumes falling independently.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:184:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:185:Key insight: Each shelf splits a stream into two at its edges, creating a branching waterfall tree.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:186:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:187:</reference_puzzle>
