/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:209:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:210:Carve color-matched motifs into solid blocks and pack them into a compact grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:211:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:212:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:213:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:214:- Several solid 5×5 monochrome blocks, each a distinct non-bg color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:215:- For each block color, a small same-colored motif sprite elsewhere on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:216:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:217:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:218:- Match each motif to its same-colored 5×5 block.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:219:- Center the motif within the block and recolor those cells to bg (punching holes).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:220:- Pack all carved blocks into an output grid preserving their original row/column order, separated by 1-cell gaps and a 1-cell outer border.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:221:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:222:Key insight: The motif acts as a stencil — it's not stamped onto the block but carved out of it as background holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:223:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:224:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:225:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:226:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="6e4f6532" lines="26-41">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:227:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:228:Dock train sprites onto station groups by matching coupler count, then orient via divider-color markers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:229:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:230:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:231:- bg; colored stripes (edge + internal) partition grid into rectangular regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:232:- Color 8 forms train bodies; color 9 marks both isolated stations and train-attached couplers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:233:- Stripe-colored pixels on trains are orientation markers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:234:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:235:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:236:- Stations = 8-connected 9-clusters not adjacent to any 8. Trains = components containing 8.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:237:- Match train to station group where |couplers| == |station size|.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:238:- Rotate/flip train so marker pixels face the same-color boundary stripe of the target region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:239:- Translate so couplers align exactly onto station cells; erase original position.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:240:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:241:Key insight: Coupler count selects the docking target; marker color encodes which boundary stripe to face, fixing the unique orientation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:242:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:243:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:244:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:245:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="38007db0" lines="9-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:246:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:247:Extract the unique cell from each lattice row into a single-column lattice.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:248:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:249:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:250:- Grid divided into equal square cells by uniform gridlines of color L.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:251:- Cell interiors filled with bg; each cell has an inner sprite pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:252:- Each row of cells has exactly one cell with a unique pattern; the rest are copies.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:253:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:254:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:255:- For each lattice row, find the cell whose inner pattern appears exactly once (the "odd one out").
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:256:- Construct a single-column lattice preserving the original row heights, containing only the unique cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:257:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:258:Key insight: The task is per-row "odd one out" — every cell in a row is identical except one oddball, which must be extracted.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:259:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:260:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:261:
