/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:263:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:264:Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:265:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:266:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:267:- The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:268:- Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:269:- Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:270:- An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:271:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:272:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:273:- For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:274:- The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:275:- For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:276:- All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:277:- A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:278:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:279:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:280:- The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:281:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:282:</reference_puzzle>
