/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:285:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:286:Simulate tokens falling through a pipe network after gates rotate open.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:287:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:288:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:289:- Wall (0), bg (pipe fill), gate (horizontal 1×3 bars), token (small edge pixels).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:290:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:291:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:292:- Rotate each gate into a vertical blocker; gate cells become bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:293:- Tokens drop downward through bg, choosing the extreme column for their side (left→min, right→max).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:294:- Tokens settle at true pipe ends (adjacent to wall/boundary), packing inward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:295:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:296:Key insight: Tokens select drop columns by entry side and land at wall-bounded endpoints, ignoring blocker-bounded ones.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:297:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:298:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:299:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:300:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="eval" puzzle_id="28a6681f" lines="8-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:301:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:302:Simulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:303:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:304:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:305:- bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:306:- Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:307:- Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:308:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:309:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:310:- Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:311:- When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:312:- When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:313:- Process repeats until no water pixel moves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:314:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:315:Key insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:316:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:317:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:318:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:319:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="3dc255db" lines="37-53">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:320:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:321:Eject content pixels from cup-shaped frames outward along each cup's tail direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:322:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:323:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:324:- bg = background. Hollow cup/Y/funnel frames, each a unique border color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:325:- Each cup has a convergent tail spike on one side and an open mouth on the opposite side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:326:- Content pixels (a single non-border color per cup) sit inside the cup's mouth interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:327:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:328:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:329:- For each cup, identify its tail spike and tail direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:330:- Erase all content pixels from the mouth interior.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:331:- Draw a straight line of content-colored pixels from the spike outward in the tail direction,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:332:  one pixel per erased content pixel; cells beyond the grid edge are dropped.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:333:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:334:Key insight: The tail spike is the unique convergent point whose outward direction is opposite
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:335:the mouth opening where the content lives.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:336:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:337:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:338:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:339:<reference_puzzle index="19" source="eval" puzzle_id="136b0064" lines="25-39">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:340:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:341:Draw a polyline by decoding 3x3 glyph instructions read across a divided grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:342:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:343:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:344:- Left of a full-height vertical divider: 3x3 colored glyphs on bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:345:- Right of divider: a single gray (5) start pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:346:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:347:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:348:- Remove the divider; shift the gray start into the left canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:349:- Read glyphs in column-major order (left→right, top→bottom).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:350:- Each glyph's shape (pixel area) encodes a segment: area 4 → down 2, area 5 → right 3, area 6 → left 4, area 7 → left 2.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:351:- Append segments sequentially, stepping down one cell between each.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:352:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:353:Key insight: Glyph pixel count (area) uniquely determines both segment length and direction — the shape itself is the instruction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:354:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:355:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:356:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:357:<reference_puzzle index="20" source="eval" puzzle_id="332f06d7" lines="9-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:358:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:359:Slide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:360:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:361:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed719905968/1/prompt.md:362:- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.
